<title>PHILIPPINES: Mabuhay says sells stake in power firm.</title>
<headline>Mabuhay says sells stake in power firm.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mabuhay Holdings Corp said on Friday it has divested its interests in power generation by forging an agreement with CEA China Inc for the sale of its stake in unlisted Magellan Capital Holdings Corp.</p>
<p>In a letter to the Philippine Stock Exchange (PSE), Mabuhay said it will sell its 1.756 million shares in Magellan for 275 million pesos. The shares represent 27 percent of Magellan's outstanding capital stocks.</p>
<p>CEA China is a member of the Public Service Enterprise Group Inc while Magellan Capital Holdings is a unit of Ultrana Energy &amp; Resources Corp.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
